        "The first month was mostly cleaning, washing bowls and carrying heavy bags of food. The animals I met were not always "
        "the cute, friendly pets I had imagined. Many had been abandoned or badly treated, and some were afraid of people. A "
        "grey dog named Duman hid at the back of his cage every time I came near. The staff told me not to force him, but simply "
        "to sit nearby and read aloud for ten minutes each visit.\n\n"
        "It felt pointless for weeks. Then one Saturday, Duman crept forward and rested his head on my shoe. I didn't move in "
        "case I frightened him, and I missed my bus home — I didn't care. Two months later, a young couple adopted him, and "
        "the manager let me be the one to put on his new collar.\n\n"
        "I finished my forty hours long ago, but I still go every Saturday. Volunteering taught me something my school never "
